ws the situation on its own."},"130":{"id":"/en-1","page_id":"/en","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en#what-tempo-does","content":"What Tempo does"},"131":{"id":"/en-2","page_id":"/en","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en#the-loop","content":"The loop"},"132":{"id":"/en-3","page_id":"/en","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en#core-principles","content":"Core principles"},"133":{"id":"/en-4","page_id":"/en","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en#next","content":"Next"},"134":{"id":"/en-5","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#what-tempo-does","content":"Tempo is a system that lets the game create crisis situations on its own. A **director** quietly\nseeds conditions — fire, rain, wind — and the **world reaction** layer picks them up and lets the\nsituation grow, the way a fire spreads. You don't have to script every scene by hand; a different\nsituation emerges every time."},"135":{"id":"/en-6","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#what-tempo-does","content":"Two games inspired it:"},"136":{"id":"/en-7","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#what-tempo-does","content":"**Left 4 Dead** — automatically adjusts the intensity (the tempo) of the action."},"137":{"id":"/en-8","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#what-tempo-does","content":"**The Legend of Zelda: BotW** — fire, water and electricity react with each other by fixed rules."},"138":{"id":"/en-9","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#what-tempo-does","content":"> **Why \"Tempo\":** what this package ultimately does is adjust the game's tension *tempo* (its rise and fall)."},"139":{"id":"/en-10","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"Every frame the three parts run in the same order: **tension → director → world**."},"140":{"id":"/en-11","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"Part"},"141":{"id":"/en-12","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"Class"},"142":{"id":"/en-13","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"Role"},"143":{"id":"/en-14","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"World reaction"},"144":{"id":"/en-15","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"`WorldReaction`"},"145":{"id":"/en-16","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"Spreads by rules on a grid; updates the list of live events"},"146":{"id":"/en-17","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"Director"},"147":{"id":"/en-18","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"`DirectorBrain`"},"148":{"id":"/en-19","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"Reads tension, picks a phase, seeds conditions within budget"},"149":{"id":"/en-20","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"Tension model"},"150":{"id":"/en-21","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"`TensionModel`"},"151":{"id":"/en-22","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#the-loop","content":"Combines player threat + nearby events into one 0–1 number"},"152":{"id":"/en-23","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#core-principles","content":"**Split the two roles.** The world reaction has no idea the director exists. It only spreads by rules."},"153":{"id":"/en-24","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#core-principles","content":"**The director never spawns enemies.** It only seeds conditions (fire, rain, wind, storm clouds upstream)."},"154":{"id":"/en-25","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#core-principles","content":"**The director watches one number** — tension (0–1): player threat combined with nearby events."},"155":{"id":"/en-26","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#core-principles","content":"**All the numbers live outside the code.** Rule tables, thresholds and weights are data a designer edits without code."},"156":{"id":"/en-27","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#next","content":"Getting started — install and your first loop."},"157":{"id":"/en-28","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#next","content":"World reaction · Director · Tension · Safeguards"},"158":{"id":"/en-29","page_id":"/en","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en#next","content":"API — the public surface, summarized."},"159":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","type":"page","content":"Idle RPG","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Use cases"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg"},"160":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-0","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","content":"AFK Arena / Legend of Mushroom — pacing auto-progress and the return moment."},"161":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-1","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"Mapping the parts"},"162":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-2","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#offline-progress-settled-in-one-pass","content":"Offline progress, settled in one pass"},"163":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-3","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mobile-checkpoints","content":"Mobile checkpoints"},"164":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-4","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","content":"> **Why it fits:** an idle game needs ups and downs even while the player isn't looking, or they don't\n> reopen it. The director shapes a tension curve to pace \"events worth coming back for.\""},"165":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-5","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"Tempo"},"166":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-6","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"In an idle RPG"},"167":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-7","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"`TensionModel`"},"168":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-8","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"Session engagement / threat curve (flat = churn, ups and downs = return)"},"169":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-9","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"`DirectorBrain` phases"},"170":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-10","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"Calm (BuildUp) → boss appears / ambush rush (Peak) → reward tally & rest (Relax)"},"171":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-11","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"`SeedAction`"},"172":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-12","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"`SpawnRaidBoss` · `TriggerGoldRush` · `AmbushEvent`"},"173":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-13","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"`WorldReaction`"},"174":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-14","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"Resource/ecology chains (vein depletes → price shifts; monsters breed → field crowds) as a rule table"},"175":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-15","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"Telegraph"},"176":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-16","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mapping-the-parts","content":"A \"boss incoming\" notice = **push-notification re-engagement**"},"177":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-17","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#offline-progress-settled-in-one-pass","content":"Idle games often don't tick every frame; they settle the \"time away\" in one pass on return. Run the three\n`Tick`s over game time (accumulated elapsed) in big steps (e.g. 1 minute = 1 tick) to replay the phase\nshifts and events that happened while away, compressed. The director only shapes the ups and downs (when a\nboss showed up); the actual combat math is handled by your idle simulation."},"178":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-18","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Ups and downs = retention.** Flat auto-progress drives churn; the director creates a reason to return with bosses/rushes."},"179":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-19","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Telegraph = push.** Wire a \"raid boss in 30 minutes\" notice to a push notification to pull players back."},"180":{"id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg-20","page_id":"/en/examples/idle-rpg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/idle-rpg#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Battery-safe.** Replay-on-return instead of per-frame simulation → zero background load."},"181":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","type":"page","content":"Match-3 puzzle","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Use cases"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/match-3"},"182":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-0","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3","content":"Royal Match / Candy Crush / Gardenscapes — the reaction rule table IS the special-tile combo table."},"183":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-1","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"Mapping the parts"},"184":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-2","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/match-3#rule-table-example","content":"Rule-table example"},"185":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-3","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/match-3#rubber-banding-with-the-director","content":"Rubber-banding with the director"},"186":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-4","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/match-3#mobile-checkpoints","content":"Mobile checkpoints"},"187":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-5","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3","content":"> **Why it fits:** the `ReactionRule` table is exactly the \"what happens when special tiles meet\" table.\n> \"Water quenches fire\" just becomes \"rocket + bomb = mega-blast\" — same structure."},"188":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-6","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"Tempo"},"189":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-7","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"In a match-3"},"190":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-8","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"`WorldReaction` grid"},"191":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-9","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"The puzzle board (cascade = grid spread)"},"192":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-10","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"`ReactionRule`"},"193":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-11","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"Special-tile combo table: Trigger=special tile, Target=neighbor tile kinds, Effect=clear/convert"},"194":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-12","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"`DataService<RuleData>`"},"195":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-13","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"Swap the table to add new special tiles = **live-ops without a code change**"},"196":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-14","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"`TensionModel`"},"197":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-15","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"Player pressure (moves left, objective progress) → difficulty rubber-banding"},"198":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-16","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"`DirectorBrain` phases"},"199":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-17","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"Easy start (BuildUp) → endgame clutch (Peak) → calm after clear (Relax)"},"200":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-18","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"`SeedAction`"},"201":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-19","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mapping-the-parts","content":"`DropGoodPiece` (a nudge when stuck) · `AddBlocker` (when too easy)"},"202":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-20","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#rule-table-example","content":"Change only the element and it becomes a match-3 combo table."},"203":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-21","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#rule-table-example","content":"`RuleValidator` catches \"unknown tile kind / conflicting rules\" before the build, so growing the table\nduring live-ops stays safe."},"204":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-22","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#rubber-banding-with-the-director","content":"The heart of match-3 is the \"barely cleared it\" feeling. The director watches tension (move-count\npressure) and seeds conditions — drop a good piece when stuck (`DropGoodPiece`), add a blocker when it's\ntoo easy. But **telegraph** (the next-piece preview) so it reads as \"see and decide,\" not \"luck.\""},"205":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-23","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**The table is live content.** Add a new event tile as one `RuleData` row, ship it via remote data with no app update."},"206":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-24","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Rubber-band subtly.** Too blatant and players notice. Ease it with `RiseSpeed`/`FallSpeed`."},"207":{"id":"/en/examples/match-3-25","page_id":"/en/examples/match-3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/match-3#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Cascades thrilling, caps clear.** A concurrent-cascade cap prevents stutter on low-end devices."},"208":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","type":"page","content":"Survivor-like","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Use cases"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/survivor-like"},"209":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-0","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like","content":"Vampire Survivors / Survivor.io / Archero — an AI director that auto-paces wave intensity."},"210":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-1","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"Mapping the parts"},"211":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-2","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#the-flow","content":"The flow"},"212":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-3","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mobile-checkpoints","content":"Mobile checkpoints"},"213":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-4","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like","content":"> **Why it fits:** this genre is essentially Left 4 Dead's \"AI Director\" by another name. Tempo's\n> tension → director → world loop *is* the swarm ↔ breather rhythm."},"214":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-5","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"Tempo"},"215":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-6","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"In a survivor-like"},"216":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-7","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"`TensionModel.Current`"},"217":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-8","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"Enemy spawn density / difficulty gauge"},"218":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-9","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"`SampleThreat`"},"219":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-10","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"On-screen enemy count + boss proximity"},"220":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-11","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"`SampleAround`"},"221":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-12","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"Ground-hazard (poison/fire/electric field) danger"},"222":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-13","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"`DirectorBrain` phases"},"223":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-14","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"Lull (BuildUp) → rush/elite (Peak) → breather (Relax)"},"224":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-15","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"`SeedAction`"},"225":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-16","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"`SpawnSwarm` · `SpawnElite` · `OpenHazardZone` · `DropHealing`"},"226":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-17","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"`WorldReaction`"},"227":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-18","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"Fire seas / poison clouds spreading on the grid (as-is)"},"228":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-19","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"Safeguard caps"},"229":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-20","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mapping-the-parts","content":"Max simultaneous enemies/hazards = **mobile heat / battery / frame defense**"},"230":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-21","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#the-flow","content":"In build-up you thin enemies and let healing/items trickle in for a breather; once tension settles low,\na rush is coming. In peak you open an elite wave plus ground hazards at once to squeeze the screen. But\nyou **must telegraph first** (wave warning ring, ground glowing red) so it never feels like a cheap death."},"231":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-22","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#the-flow","content":"`SpawnSwarm`/`SpawnElite` don't spawn enemies directly — they seed **spawn conditions** (open a spawn\ngate); your game's pooling/placement picks them up. The director only decides *when* and *how much*."},"232":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-23","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Caps are your perf budget.** `MaxActiveEvents` and a concurrent-enemy cap protect frames on low-end devices."},"233":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-24","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Sessions are short.** Keep phase cycles around 1–2 minutes so build-up → peak → relax loops several times per run."},"234":{"id":"/en/examples/survivor-like-25","page_id":"/en/examples/survivor-like","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/survivor-like#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Telegraph big.** On a small screen warnings get lost; make them obvious with rings / screen-edge reddening."},"235":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","type":"page","content":"Tower defense","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Use cases"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/tower-defense"},"236":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-0","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense","content":"Random Dice / defense games — auto-paced waves + status-effect chains."},"237":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-1","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"Mapping the parts"},"238":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-2","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#status-chains-are-elemental-reactions","content":"Status chains *are* elemental reactions"},"239":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-3","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mobile-checkpoints","content":"Mobile checkpoints"},"240":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-4","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense","content":"> **Why it fits:** two things click at once — the director's wave pacing (Left 4 Dead) and freeze/shock\n> chaining through enemy crowds (BotW's electric chain, verbatim)."},"241":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-5","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"Tempo"},"242":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-6","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"In a tower defense"},"243":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-7","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"`TensionModel`"},"244":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-8","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"Defense-line pressure (leaked enemies, core HP)"},"245":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-9","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"`DirectorBrain` phases"},"246":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-10","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"Scout (BuildUp) → rush/special mob (Peak) → regroup (Relax)"},"247":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-11","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"`SeedAction`"},"248":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-12","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"`SeedColdSnap` (freeze field) · `ChargeStorm` (shock chain) · `SpawnRusher`"},"249":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-13","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"`WorldReaction`"},"250":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-14","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"Status propagation: freeze/shock jumps from an afflicted enemy to neighbors (elemental reaction as-is)"},"251":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-15","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"Safeguard caps"},"252":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-16","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mapping-the-parts","content":"Concurrent enemy/projectile cap = mobile frame defense"},"253":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-17","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#status-chains-are-elemental-reactions","content":"BotW's \"electricity travels through metal\" rule maps straight onto a defense game's \"shock chains through\nwet/metal enemy crowds.\" Just read the `ReactionRule` table as enemy status effects."},"254":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-18","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#status-chains-are-elemental-reactions","content":"When the line is too easy (low tension) the director seeds rushes/special mobs to squeeze; when it's\noverwhelmed (high) it gives breathing room. \"Elemental combos\" — luring a shock onto a freeze field the\nplayer laid down — fall out of the same table naturally."},"255":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-19","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Combos are the feel.** Keep chains like freeze → shock in the rule table to add new combos as data, live."},"256":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-20","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Wave pacing = the difficulty curve.** The director adjusts pressure without you hand-authoring every stage."},"257":{"id":"/en/examples/tower-defense-21","page_id":"/en/examples/tower-defense","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/examples/tower-defense#mobile-checkpoints","content":"**Caps = performance.** A concurrent enemy/projectile cap keeps frames steady even in late-game swarms."},"258":{"id":"/en/usage/director","page_id":"/en/usage/director","type":"page","content":"Director","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Usage"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/director"},"259":{"id":"/en/usage/director-0","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director","content":"Reads one tension number, picks a phase, and seeds only conditions within budget."},"260":{"id":"/en/usage/director-1","page_id":"/en/usage/director","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"One seed action — `SeedAction`"},"261":{"id":"/en/usage/director-2","page_id":"/en/usage/director","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/director#the-directors-brain--directorbrain","content":"The director's brain — `DirectorBrain`"},"262":{"id":"/en/usage/director-3","page_id":"/en/usage/director","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/director#phases-and-budget","content":"Phases and budget"},"263":{"id":"/en/usage/director-4","page_id":"/en/usage/director","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/director#no-flicker--phasefsm","content":"No flicker — `PhaseFsm`"},"264":{"id":"/en/usage/director-5","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director","content":"The director never spawns enemies. It reads a single tension number, picks a phase\n(build-up → peak → relax), and then, within its budget, picks actions that seed **only conditions** into the world."},"265":{"id":"/en/usage/director-6","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"`Intent` ties to a phase — **Prepare** (build-up), **Trigger** (peak), **Calm** (relax). Each action\nfirst checks `CanSeed` (\"is it OK to seed now?\") and only calls the world's entry points\n(`ApplyElement` / `SetWind`)."},"266":{"id":"/en/usage/director-7","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"The four built-ins:"},"267":{"id":"/en/usage/director-8","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Action"},"268":{"id":"/en/usage/director-9","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Intent"},"269":{"id":"/en/usage/director-10","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Role"},"270":{"id":"/en/usage/director-11","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"`DryUpwind`"},"271":{"id":"/en/usage/director-12","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Prepare"},"272":{"id":"/en/usage/director-13","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Raises and dries the wind to set up good spread (no fire yet)"},"273":{"id":"/en/usage/director-14","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"`IgniteUpwind`"},"274":{"id":"/en/usage/director-15","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Trigger"},"275":{"id":"/en/usage/director-16","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Throws an ember into dry grass upwind → it rides the wind toward the player"},"276":{"id":"/en/usage/director-17","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"`ChargeStorm`"},"277":{"id":"/en/usage/director-18","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Trigger"},"278":{"id":"/en/usage/director-19","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Floats a storm cloud over metal/puddles to shock"},"279":{"id":"/en/usage/director-20","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"`SummonRain`"},"280":{"id":"/en/usage/director-21","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Calm"},"281":{"id":"/en/usage/director-22","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#one-seed-action--seedaction","content":"Rains to quench and wet, giving a breather"},"282":{"id":"/en/usage/director-23","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#the-directors-brain--directorbrain","content":"Use `DefaultDirectorBrain` to run with no overrides."},"283":{"id":"/en/usage/director-24","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#phases-and-budget","content":"Each phase gives the director a different budget, declared in `PhaseData`."},"284":{"id":"/en/usage/director-25","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#phases-and-budget","content":"**BuildUp** — stack only good-spread conditions (dry grass, charge, fuel). Small budget, nothing dangerous."},"285":{"id":"/en/usage/director-26","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#phases-and-budget","content":"**Peak** — on top of what's stacked, throw an ember so it all goes up. Spend a lot."},"286":{"id":"/en/usage/director-27","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#phases-and-budget","content":"**Relax** — rain to quench and catch a breath while budget recovers. Calming actions only."},"287":{"id":"/en/usage/director-28","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#phases-and-budget","content":"The default `PickActions` picks actions whose `Intent` matches the phase, within budget, that pass\n`CanSeed`. Override it when you need finer policy."},"288":{"id":"/en/usage/director-29","page_id":"/en/usage/director","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/director#no-flicker--phasefsm","content":"With a single threshold the phase flickers at the boundary. So the enter and exit thresholds differ\n(hysteresis), and a minimum relax time is guaranteed."},"289":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","type":"page","content":"Safeguards","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Usage"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/safeguards"},"290":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-0","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards","content":"Keep chains from growing too big, and always telegraph what the director seeds."},"291":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-1","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/safeguards#1-caps","content":"1\\. Caps"},"292":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-2","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/safeguards#2-quench-first-in-the-relax-phase","content":"2\\. Quench first in the relax phase"},"293":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-3","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/safeguards#3-mercy-when-it-goes-off-underfoot","content":"3\\. Mercy when it goes off underfoot"},"294":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-4","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/safeguards#4-telegraph-it-foreshadowing","content":"4\\. Telegraph it (foreshadowing)"},"295":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-5","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/safeguards#checking-with-debug-tools","content":"Checking with debug tools"},"296":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-6","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards","content":"The world can produce chains even the director didn't expect. A few safeguards keep it in check."},"297":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-7","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#1-caps","content":"Cap the number / total magnitude of simultaneous events. Past the cap, hold off on lighting new fires\n(Trigger actions)."},"298":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-8","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#1-caps","content":"`WorldReaction.BurningCells` also exposes the burning-cell count for a stricter cap."},"299":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-9","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#2-quench-first-in-the-relax-phase","content":"In the relax phase only `Intent == Calm` actions (rain, extinguish) are chosen. The default policy\nalready behaves this way."},"300":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-10","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#3-mercy-when-it-goes-off-underfoot","content":"So a condition the director seeded doesn't kill the player instantly right underfoot, ease off near the\nplayer — reduce the power or delay it a beat. (This is where your damage code applies a distance falloff.)"},"301":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-11","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#4-telegraph-it-foreshadowing","content":"The most important one. Conditions the director seeds **must be telegraphed** — storm clouds gather,\nthe wind dries out. Without it the player just thinks \"why did I suddenly die?\""},"302":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-12","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#4-telegraph-it-foreshadowing","content":"`DryUpwind` → wind picking up and drying (rustling grass, sound)."},"303":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-13","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#4-telegraph-it-foreshadowing","content":"`ChargeStorm` → storm clouds gathering first."},"304":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-14","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#4-telegraph-it-foreshadowing","content":"`IgniteUpwind` → a small ember/smoke visible upwind in the distance first."},"305":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-15","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#4-telegraph-it-foreshadowing","content":"Read `DirectorBrain.CurrentPhase` and `WorldReaction.ActiveEvents` to drive your foreshadowing visuals."},"306":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-16","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#4-telegraph-it-foreshadowing","content":"> **Why it matters:** BotW used sleight-of-hand tricks, yet still showed clearly what needed showing.\n> Ultima Online's autonomous ecology, by contrast, failed because players never noticed it.\n> &#x2A;*Show clearly what needs to be shown.**"},"307":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-17","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#checking-with-debug-tools","content":"Use the editor's **Tools → Tempo → Debug Window** to watch the tension graph, phase, event count and\nburning cells live. Wire it up from your game code:"},"308":{"id":"/en/usage/safeguards-18","page_id":"/en/usage/safeguards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/safeguards#checking-with-debug-tools","content":"Before building, **Tools → Tempo → Validate Rules** (or the automatic build check) catches missing\nmaterials and conflicting rules in the table."},"309":{"id":"/en/usage/tension","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","type":"page","content":"Tension","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Usage"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/tension"},"310":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-0","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension","content":"The model that combines player threat and nearby activity into a single 0–1 number."},"311":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-1","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/tension#the-three-steps","content":"The three steps"},"312":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-2","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/tension#public-surface","content":"Public surface"},"313":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-3","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/tension#damage-is-immediate-threat-is-gradual","content":"Damage is immediate, threat is gradual"},"314":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-4","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/tension#injecting-signals-for-tests","content":"Injecting signals for tests"},"315":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-5","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"Tuning — `TensionConfig`"},"316":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-6","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension","content":"All the director watches is one number: tension (0–1). `TensionModel` builds it in three steps:\n&#x2A;*normalize the two signals to 0–1 → combine → smooth.**"},"317":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-7","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#the-three-steps","content":"**Normalize** — bring player threat and nearby activity each into the 0–1 range."},"318":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-8","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#the-three-steps","content":"**Combine** — if either is high the whole thing rises; if both are high it's near the max (never over 1).\nThe formula is `1-(1-a)(1-b)`."},"319":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-9","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#the-three-steps","content":"**Smooth** — rise fast, fall slow. Danger should register immediately; relief should arrive gradually."},"320":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-10","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#the-three-steps","content":"> **Two ways to combine**\n>\n> * Default: `1-(1-a)(1-b)`.\n> * Sharper: just the larger of the two, `Mathf.Max(a, b)`.\n>\n> **The key is \"rise fast, fall slow.\"** That's what makes the build-up → peak → relax flow feel natural."},"321":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-11","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#damage-is-immediate-threat-is-gradual","content":"Inside `Tick`, closer threats accumulate more, and stress decays gradually over time."},"322":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-12","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#injecting-signals-for-tests","content":"The two sample methods are `virtual`, so a test can inject signals directly without a physics scene\n(swapped in place of an interface)."},"323":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-13","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#injecting-signals-for-tests","content":"The default `SampleThreat` counts nearby enemies via `Physics.OverlapSphere`; `SampleAround` weights\n`world.ActiveEvents` so that closer, bigger events count more."},"324":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-14","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"Strengths, radii, weights, speeds and thresholds are all data. Tune the ranges in your game."},"325":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-15","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"Value"},"326":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-16","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"Meaning"},"327":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-17","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"`DamageGain`"},"328":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-18","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"Immediate spike on hit"},"329":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-19","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"`ThreatGain` / `StressDecay`"},"330":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-20","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"Threat accumulation / stress decay"},"331":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-21","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"`StressWeight` / `AroundWeight`"},"332":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-22","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"Weights when combining the two signals"},"333":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-23","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"`RiseSpeed` / `FallSpeed`"},"334":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-24","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"Time constants for rising / falling"},"335":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-25","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"`ThreatRadius` / `AroundRadius`"},"336":{"id":"/en/usage/tension-26","page_id":"/en/usage/tension","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/tension#tuning--tensionconfig","content":"Sampling radii"},"337":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","type":"page","content":"World reaction","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Usage"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/world-reaction"},"338":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-0","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction","content":"The side where fire, water and electricity transform by rules and spread across a grid."},"339":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-1","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#one-cells-state--elementalstate","content":"One cell's state — `ElementalState`"},"340":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-2","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#materialdef","content":"MaterialDef"},"341":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-3","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#reaction-rule--reactionrule","content":"Reaction rule — `ReactionRule`"},"342":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-4","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#spread-and-results--worldreaction","content":"Spread and results — `WorldReaction`"},"343":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-5","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#laying-down-a-grid","content":"Laying down a grid"},"344":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-6","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#seeding-conditions-directly","content":"Seeding conditions directly"},"345":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-7","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction","content":"The world reaction has no idea the director exists. Conditions come in, it spreads by rules, and it\nkeeps the list of live events up to date."},"346":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-8","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#one-cells-state--elementalstate","content":"The current state of a cell (or object). It's a lightweight `struct` because the grid processes many of them."},"347":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-9","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#one-cells-state--elementalstate","content":"Fixed properties — flammability, conductivity, melting point — aren't stored in the state; they're\nlooked up from `MaterialDef`."},"348":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-10","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#materialdef","content":"Materials are registered once and shared by index. `RuleData.ResolveMaterialId(name)` finds one by name,\ncreating and registering it if missing."},"349":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-11","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#reaction-rule--reactionrule","content":"Reactions are data, not code: \"this element / touching this material / over this threshold → changes like this\"."},"350":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-12","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#reaction-rule--reactionrule","content":"Target materials go in &#x2A;*one field separated by `;`**, not an array UI (a project convention). They're\nsplit once and cached. Leave it empty to match every material."},"351":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-13","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#reaction-rule--reactionrule","content":"The three BotW rules are the starting point:"},"352":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-14","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#reaction-rule--reactionrule","content":"an element changes a **material** — fire burns dry grass;"},"353":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-15","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#reaction-rule--reactionrule","content":"an element changes **another element** — water quenches fire;"},"354":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-16","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#reaction-rule--reactionrule","content":"depending on the situation an element creates a **force** — electricity shocks through metal."},"355":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-17","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#reaction-rule--reactionrule","content":"The rule table comes from `DataService<RuleData>.GetDataCenter()`."},"356":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-18","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#spread-and-results--worldreaction","content":"**How it spreads:** rules are applied on a flat grid (a plain array / `Dictionary`, never a `SortedSet`)\nso fire jumps to neighbor cells. It spreads each frame based on wind direction and how flammable the\nneighbor is."},"357":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-19","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#spread-and-results--worldreaction","content":"**`ActiveEvents`:** each entry is a `ReactionEvent` (position, magnitude, time-to-live, kind). The\ndirector and tension model watch this list. Finished entries are cleared each frame, and nearby events\nof the same kind merge into one."},"358":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-20","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#seeding-conditions-directly","content":"`ApplyElement` applies the rule table to the touched cells immediately (water touching fire quenches it\nright there); `Tick` then carries the spread forward."},"359":{"id":"/en/usage/world-reaction-21","page_id":"/en/usage/world-reaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/world-reaction#seeding-conditions-directly","content":"> Performance: grid math also fits Jobs/Burst + `NativeArray`. The default implementation uses a managed\n> flat array so it runs with no dependencies."}},"count":359},"sorting":{"language":"english","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":163,"2":322,"3":46,"4":134,"5":347,"6":43,"7":63,"8":45,"9":120,"10":42,"11":44,"12":154,"13":230,"14":282,"15":183,"16":49,"17":84,"18":219,"19":52,"20":82,"21":179,"22":50,"23":40,"24":291,"25":112,"26":38,"27":281,"28":76,"29":37,"30":217,"31":79,"32":36,"33":263,"34":127,"35":35,"36":288,"37":71,"38":95,"39":85,"40":97,"41":72,"42":75,"43":231,"44":283,"45":184,"46":56,"47":88,"48":309,"49":128,"50":41,"51":252,"52":48,"53":132,"54":308,"55":91,"56":130,"57":156,"58":86,"59":131,"60":285,"61":61,"62":110,"63":168,"64":74,"65":73,"66":90,"67":232,"68":284,"69":185,"70":55,"71":77,"72":307,"73":92,"74":78,"75":254,"76":87,"77":34,"78":202,"79":129,"80":39,"81":343,