":276,"290":216,"291":149,"292":150,"293":151,"294":152,"295":174,"296":329,"297":171,"298":133,"299":210,"300":286,"301":320,"302":70,"303":54,"304":81,"305":262,"306":146,"307":345,"308":166,"309":305,"310":319,"311":327,"312":256,"313":180,"314":211,"315":339,"316":159,"317":15,"318":7,"319":21,"320":140,"321":212,"322":328,"323":312,"324":294,"325":346,"326":229,"327":57,"328":203,"329":125,"330":332,"331":116,"332":349,"333":98,"334":335,"335":126,"336":277,"337":355,"338":325,"339":245,"340":226,"341":260,"342":289,"343":218,"344":279,"345":330,"346":310,"347":195,"348":227,"349":261,"350":298,"351":326,"352":162,"353":161,"354":182,"355":324,"356":13,"357":0,"358":51,"359":147},"orderedDocs":[[357,"**`ActiveEvents`:** each entry is a `ReactionEvent` (position, magnitude, time-to-live, kind). The\ndirector and tension model watch this list. Finished entries are cleared each frame, and nearby events\nof the same kind merge into one."],[155,"**All the numbers live outside the code.** Rule tables, thresholds and weights are data a designer edits without code."],[180,"**Battery-safe.** Replay-on-return instead of per-frame simulation → zero background load."],[284,"**BuildUp** — stack only good-spread conditions (dry grass, charge, fuel). Small budget, nothing dangerous."],[257,"**Caps = performance.** A concurrent enemy/projectile cap keeps frames steady even in late-game swarms."],[232,"**Caps are your perf budget.** `MaxActiveEvents` and a concurrent-enemy cap protect frames on low-end devices."],[207,"**Cascades thrilling, caps clear.** A concurrent-cascade cap prevents stutter on low-end devices."],[318,"**Combine** — if either is high the whole thing rises; if both are high it's near the max (never over 1).\nThe formula is `1-(1-a)(1-b)`."],[255,"**Combos are the feel.** Keep chains like freeze → shock in the rule table to add new combos as data, live."],[103,"**Config** (`Achieve.Tempo.Config`): the code-separated data center `DataService<T>` and\n`TensionConfig`/`PhaseData`/`ActionData`/`RuleData` (with defaults)."],[101,"**Director** (`Achieve.Tempo.Director`): `DirectorBrain` with a default policy extended via `virtual`,\nthe `SeedAction` seeding action plus four built-ins (`DryUpwind`/`IgniteUpwind`/`ChargeStorm`/`SummonRain`),\nand `PhaseFsm` phase switching (hysteresis)."],[107,"**Docs**: fumadocs site (ko/en/ja/zh)."],[104,"**Editor tools** (`Achieve.Tempo.Editor`): `RuleValidator` (pre-build rule-table check) and\n`DebugWindow` (live tension/phase view)."],[356,"**How it spreads:** rules are applied on a flat grid (a plain array / `Dictionary`, never a `SortedSet`)\nso fire jumps to neighbor cells. It spreads each frame based on wind direction and how flammable the\nneighbor is."],[136,"**Left 4 Dead** — automatically adjusts the intensity (the tempo) of the action."],[317,"**Normalize** — bring player threat and nearby activity each into the 0–1 range."],[285,"**Peak** — on top of what's stacked, throw an ember so it all goes up. Spend a lot."],[286,"**Relax** — rain to quench and catch a breath while budget recovers. Calming actions only."],[206,"**Rubber-band subtly.** Too blatant and players notice. Ease it with `RiseSpeed`/`FallSpeed`."],[106,"**Sample**: `Samples~/BasicGrassFire` — the simplest single loop."],[233,"**Sessions are short.** Keep phase cycles around 1–2 minutes so build-up → peak → relax loops several times per run."],[319,"**Smooth** — rise fast, fall slow. Danger should register immediately; relief should arrive gradually."],[152,"**Split the two roles.** The world reaction has no idea the director exists. It only spreads by rules."],[179,"**Telegraph = push.** Wire a \"raid boss in 30 minutes\" notice to a push notification to pull players back."],[234,"**Telegraph big.** On a small screen warnings get lost; make them obvious with rings / screen-edge reddening."],[102,"**Tension** (`Achieve.Tempo.Tension`): `TensionModel` combining two signals into 0–1 (rise fast, fall slow)."],[105,"**Tests**: EditMode (`TensionModel`/`PhaseFsm`/`ReactionRule`/`RuleValidator`),\nPlayMode (spread direction, quench, event cleanup)."],[153,"**The director never spawns enemies.** It only seeds conditions (fire, rain, wind, storm clouds upstream)."],[154,"**The director watches one number** — tension (0–1): player threat combined with nearby events."],[137,"**The Legend of Zelda: BotW** — fire, water and electricity react with each other by fixed rules."],[205,"**The table is live content.** Add a new event tile as one `RuleData` row, ship it via remote data with no app update."],[178,"**Ups and downs = retention.** Flat auto-progress drives churn; the director creates a reason to return with bosses/rushes."],[256,"**Wave pacing = the difficulty curve.** The director adjusts pressure without you hand-authoring every stage."],[100,"**World reaction** (`Achieve.Tempo.World`): `WorldReaction` spreading fire/water/ice/electricity by\nrules on a flat grid, per-cell `ElementalState`, `MaterialDef`, table-driven `ReactionRule`\n(single-field `;` input), and the live-event `ReactionEvent`."],[77,"`(float dmg, float maxHp)`"],[35,"`(float dt)`"],[32,"`(int x, int y) → ElementalState`"],[29,"`(string material)` / `(int x, int y, string material)`"],[26,"`(Vector2 dir, float strength)`"],[80,"`(Vector3 playerPos, WorldReaction, float dt)`"],[23,"`(Vector3 pos, float radius, ElementTag e, float power)`"],[50,"`(WorldReaction, TensionModel, Vector3 playerPos, float dt)`"],[10,"`Achieve.Tempo.Config`"],[6,"`Achieve.Tempo.Director`"],[11,"`Achieve.Tempo.Editor`"],[8,"`Achieve.Tempo.Tension`"],[3,"`Achieve.Tempo.World`"],[91,"`ActionData` — `Actions`, `Add(SeedAction)`."],[52,"`ActionPool`"],[16,"`ActiveEvents`"],[22,"`ApplyElement`"],[358,"`ApplyElement` applies the rule table to the touched cells immediately (water touching fire quenches it\nright there); `Tick` then carries the spread forward."],[19,"`BurningCells`"],[276,"`ChargeStorm`"],[303,"`ChargeStorm` → storm clouds gathering first."],[70,"`Current`"],[46,"`CurrentPhase`"],[327,"`DamageGain`"],[194,"`DataService<RuleData>`"],[88,"`DataService<T>` — `GetDataCenter()`, `Register(T)`, `Reset()`."],[94,"`DebugWindow` — `Bind(TensionModel, DirectorBrain, WorldReaction)`, menu `Tools/Tempo/Debug Window`."],[61,"`DefaultDirectorBrain` — default implementation to use without overrides."],[147,"`DirectorBrain`"],[7,"`DirectorBrain` (abstract)"],[169,"`DirectorBrain` phases"],[198,"`DirectorBrain` phases"],[222,"`DirectorBrain` phases"],[245,"`DirectorBrain` phases"],[201,"`DropGoodPiece` (a nudge when stuck) · `AddBlocker` (when too easy)"],[270,"`DryUpwind`"],[302,"`DryUpwind` → wind picking up and drying (rustling grass, sound)."],[37,"`ElementalState` (struct) — `MaterialId, Temperature, Wetness, Charge, OnFire, Frozen`"],[41,"`enum ElementTag` — `None, Fire, Water, Ice, Electric, Wind`"],[65,"`enum Phase` — `BuildUp, Peak, Relax`."],[64,"`enum SeedIntent` — `Prepare, Trigger, Calm`."],[42,"`enum StateEffect` — `Ignite, Extinguish, Wet, Dry, Freeze, Thaw, Charge, Discharge`"],[28,"`Fill` / `SetCell`"],[71,"`float`"],[74,"`float`"],[31,"`GetCell`"],[273,"`IgniteUpwind`"],[304,"`IgniteUpwind` → a small ember/smoke visible upwind in the distance first."],[20,"`int`"],[265,"`Intent` ties to a phase — **Prepare** (build-up), **Trigger** (peak), **Calm** (relax). Each action\nfirst checks `CanSeed` (\"is it OK to seed now?\") and only calls the world's entry points\n(`ApplyElement` / `SetWind`)."],[17,"`IReadOnlyList<ReactionEvent>`"],[39,"`MaterialDef` — `Name, Flammability, Conductivity, IgnitionPoint, FreezePoint, WaterAbsorption`"],[58,"`MaxActiveEvents`"],[76,"`OnPlayerDamaged`"],[47,"`Phase`"],[90,"`PhaseData` — `PeakEnter/RelaxEnter/BuildUpEnter/MinRelax`, per-phase budgets, `BudgetFor(Phase)`."],[66,"`PhaseFsm` — `Evaluate(float tension, float dt) → Phase`, `Current`, `Reset()`."],[55,"`PickActions`"],[73,"`PlayerStress`"],[86,"`protected virtual (Vector3, WorldReaction) → float`"],[83,"`protected virtual (Vector3) → float`"],[38,"`ReactionEvent` (struct) — `Position, Magnitude, Ttl, Kind`"],[192,"`ReactionRule`"],[40,"`ReactionRule` — `Trigger, TargetMaterials(;), Effect, Probability, Threshold`, `TargetMaterialList`, `MatchesMaterial`, static `Split`"],[333,"`RiseSpeed` / `FallSpeed`"],[92,"`RuleData` — `Materials`, `Rules`, `ResolveMaterialId`, `GetMaterial`, `AddMaterial`, `AddRule`, spread thresholds."],[93,"`RuleValidator` — `Validate(RuleData) → List<Issue>`, menu `Tools/Tempo/Validate Rules`, automatic pre-build check."],[203,"`RuleValidator` catches \"unknown tile kind / conflicting rules\" before the build, so growing the table\nduring live-ops stays safe."],[85,"`SampleAround`"],[220,"`SampleAround`"],[82,"`SampleThreat`"],[218,"`SampleThreat`"],[171,"`SeedAction`"],[200,"`SeedAction`"],[224,"`SeedAction`"],[247,"`SeedAction`"],[62,"`SeedAction` (abstract) — `Cost`, `Intent`, `CanSeed`, `Seed`."],[248,"`SeedColdSnap` (freeze field) · `ChargeStorm` (shock chain) · `SpawnRusher`"],[25,"`SetWind`"],[172,"`SpawnRaidBoss` · `TriggerGoldRush` · `AmbushEvent`"],[225,"`SpawnSwarm` · `SpawnElite` · `OpenHazardZone` · `DropHealing`"],[231,"`SpawnSwarm`/`SpawnElite` don't spawn enemies directly — they seed **spawn conditions** (open a spawn\ngate); your game's pooling/placement picks them up. The director only decides *when* and *how much*."],[331,"`StressWeight` / `AroundWeight`"],[279,"`SummonRain`"],[89,"`TensionConfig` — strengths, radii, weights, speeds, thresholds."],[216,"`TensionModel.Current`"],[9,"`TensionModel`"],[150,"`TensionModel`"],[167,"`TensionModel`"],[196,"`TensionModel`"],[243,"`TensionModel`"],[329,"`ThreatGain` / `StressDecay`"],[335,"`ThreatRadius` / `AroundRadius`"],[34,"`Tick`"],[49,"`Tick`"],[79,"`Tick`"],[56,"`virtual IEnumerable<SeedAction>`"],[59,"`virtual int`"],[53,"`virtual IReadOnlyList<SeedAction>`"],[298,"`WorldReaction.BurningCells` also exposes the burning-cell count for a stricter cap."],[4,"`WorldReaction`"],[144,"`WorldReaction`"],[173,"`WorldReaction`"],[226,"`WorldReaction`"],[249,"`WorldReaction`"],[190,"`WorldReaction` grid"],[320,"> **Two ways to combine**\n>\n> * Default: `1-(1-a)(1-b)`.\n> * Sharper: just the larger of the two, `Mathf.Max(a, b)`.\n>\n> **The key is \"rise fast, fall slow.\"** That's what makes the build-up → peak → relax flow feel natural."],[138,"> **Why \"Tempo\":** what this package ultimately does is adjust the game's tension *tempo* (its rise and fall)."],[164,"> **Why it fits:** an idle game needs ups and downs even while the player isn't looking, or they don't\n> reopen it. The director shapes a tension curve to pace \"events worth coming back for.\""],[187,"> **Why it fits:** the `ReactionRule` table is exactly the \"what happens when special tiles meet\" table.\n> \"Water quenches fire\" just becomes \"rocket + bomb = mega-blast\" — same structure."],[213,"> **Why it fits:** this genre is essentially Left 4 Dead's \"AI Director\" by another name. Tempo's\n> tension → director → world loop *is* the swarm ↔ breather rhythm."],[240,"> **Why it fits:** two things click at once — the director's wave pacing (Left 4 Dead) and freeze/shock\n> chaining through enemy crowds (BotW's electric chain, verbatim)."],[306,"> **Why it matters:** BotW used sleight-of-hand tricks, yet still showed clearly what needed showing.\n> Ultima Online's autonomous ecology, by contrast, failed because players never noticed it.\n> &#x2A;*Show clearly what needs to be shown.**"],[359,"> Performance: grid math also fits Jobs/Burst + `NativeArray`. The default implementation uses a managed\n> flat array so it runs with no dependencies."],[97,"1.0.0 — 2026-06-27"],[291,"1\\. Caps"],[292,"2\\. Quench first in the relax phase"],[293,"3\\. Mercy when it goes off underfoot"],[294,"4\\. Telegraph it (foreshadowing)"],[176,"A \"boss incoming\" notice = **push-notification re-engagement**"],[12,"A game typically subclasses `DirectorBrain`, swaps the action list, and calls the three `Tick`s from its own loop."],[267,"Action"],[57,"Action-selection policy (override)"],[98,"Added"],[160,"AFK Arena / Legend of Mushroom — pacing auto-progress and the return moment."],[316,"All the director watches is one number: tension (0–1). `TensionModel` builds it in three steps:\n&#x2A;*normalize the two signals to 0–1 → combine → smooth.**"],[129,"An automatic tension-pacing system where the director only seeds conditions and the world grows the situation on its own."],[353,"an element changes **another element** — water quenches fire;"],[352,"an element changes a **material** — fire burns dry grass;"],[1,"API"],[158,"API — the public surface, summarized."],[121,"Attach this component to an empty `GameObject` and a grass fire starts spreading."],[308,"Before building, **Tools → Tempo → Validate Rules** (or the automatic build check) catches missing\nmaterials and conflicting rules in the table."],[253,"BotW's \"electricity travels through metal\" rule maps straight onto a defense game's \"shock chains through\nwet/metal enemy crowds.\" Just read the `ReactionRule` table as enemy status effects."],[63,"Built-in actions: `DryUpwind`, `IgniteUpwind`, `ChargeStorm`, `SummonRain`."],[280,"Calm"],[170,"Calm (BuildUp) → boss appears / ambush rush (Peak) → reward tally & rest (Relax)"],[297,"Cap the number / total magnitude of simultaneous events. Past the cap, hold off on lighting new fires\n(Trigger actions)."],[202,"Change only the element and it becomes a match-3 combo table."],[95,"Changelog"],[295,"Checking with debug tools"],[141,"Class"],[151,"Combines player threat + nearby events into one 0–1 number"],[252,"Concurrent enemy/projectile cap = mobile frame defense"],[132,"Core principles"],[21,"Currently burning cell count"],[313,"Damage is immediate, threat is gradual"],[244,"Defense-line pressure (leaked enemies, core HP)"],[354,"depending on the situation an element creates a **force** — electricity shocks through metal."],[15,"Description"],[45,"Description"],[69,"Description"],[146,"Director"],[258,"Director"],[127,"Director to customize phases and actions."],[283,"Each phase gives the director a different budget, declared in `PhaseData`."],[199,"Easy start (BuildUp) → endgame clutch (Peak) → calm after clear (Relax)"],[217,"Enemy spawn density / difficulty gauge"],[139,"Every frame the three parts run in the same order: **tension → director → world**."],[113,"Feeding damage into tension"],[227,"Fire seas / poison clouds spreading on the grid (as-is)"],[347,"Fixed properties — flammability, conductivity, melting point — aren't stored in the state; they're\nlooked up from `MaterialDef`."],[278,"Floats a storm cloud over metal/puddles to shock"],[108,"Getting started"],[156,"Getting started — install and your first loop."],[221,"Ground-hazard (poison/fire/electric field) danger"],[177,"Idle games often don't tick every frame; they settle the \"time away\" in one pass on return. Run the three\n`Tick`s over game time (accumulated elapsed) in big steps (e.g. 1 minute = 1 tick) to replay the phase\nshifts and events that happened while away, compressed. The director only shapes the ups and downs (when a\nboss showed up); the actual combat math is handled by your idle simulation."],[159,"Idle RPG"],[78,"Immediate spike on hit"],[328,"Immediate spike on hit"],[115,"Import the sample"],[189,"In a match-3"],[215,"In a survivor-like"],[242,"In a tower defense"],[166,"In an idle RPG"],[230,"In build-up you thin enemies and let healing/items trickle in for a breather; once tension settles low,\na rush is coming. In peak you open an elite wave plus ground hazards at once to squeeze the screen. But\nyou **must telegraph first** (wave warning ring, ground glowing red) so it never feels like a cheap death."],[299,"In the relax phase only `Intent == Calm` actions (rain, extinguish) are chosen. The default policy\nalready behaves this way."],[314,"Injecting signals for tests"],[321,"Inside `Tick`, closer threats accumulate more, and