data. Tune the ranges in your game."],[208,"Survivor-like"],[195,"Swap the table to add new special tiles = **live-ops without a code change**"],[114,"Swapping data"],[350,"Target materials go in &#x2A;*one field separated by `;`**, not an array UI (a project convention). They're\nsplit once and cached. Leave it empty to match every material."],[175,"Telegraph"],[165,"Tempo"],[188,"Tempo"],[214,"Tempo"],[241,"Tempo"],[134,"Tempo is a system that lets the game create crisis situations on its own. A **director** quietly\nseeds conditions — fire, rain, wind — and the **world reaction** layer picks them up and lets the\nsituation grow, the way a fire spreads. You don't have to script every scene by hand; a different\nsituation emerges every time."],[309,"Tension"],[149,"Tension model"],[72,"Tension the director reads, 0–1"],[54,"The action list (override)"],[48,"The current phase"],[346,"The current state of a cell (or object). It's a lightweight `struct` because the grid processes many of them."],[287,"The default `PickActions` picks actions whose `Intent` matches the phase, within budget, that pass\n`CanSeed`. Override it when you need finer policy."],[323,"The default `SampleThreat` counts nearby enemies via `Physics.OverlapSphere`; `SampleAround` weights\n`world.ActiveEvents` so that closer, bigger events count more."],[264,"The director never spawns enemies. It reads a single tension number, picks a phase\n(build-up → peak → relax), and then, within its budget, picks actions that seed **only conditions** into the world."],[261,"The director's brain — `DirectorBrain`"],[211,"The flow"],[266,"The four built-ins:"],[204,"The heart of match-3 is the \"barely cleared it\" feeling. The director watches tension (move-count\npressure) and seeds conditions — drop a good piece when stuck (`DropGoodPiece`), add a blocker when it's\ntoo easy. But **telegraph** (the next-piece preview) so it reads as \"see and decide,\" not \"luck.\""],[131,"The loop"],[310,"The model that combines player threat and nearby activity into a single 0–1 number."],[301,"The most important one. Conditions the director seeds **must be telegraphed** — storm clouds gather,\nthe wind dries out. Without it the player just thinks \"why did I suddenly die?\""],[122,"The order of the three `Tick` calls is **always** tension → director → world. The director reads this\nframe's tension and seeds conditions; the world picks them up and spreads."],[2,"The public classes and members, summarized."],[191,"The puzzle board (cascade = grid spread)"],[355,"The rule table comes from `DataService<RuleData>.GetDataCenter()`."],[338,"The side where fire, water and electricity transform by rules and spread across a grid."],[351,"The three BotW rules are the starting point:"],[311,"The three steps"],[322,"The two sample methods are `virtual`, so a test can inject signals directly without a physics scene\n(swapped in place of an interface)."],[296,"The world can produce chains even the director didn't expect. A few safeguards keep it in check."],[345,"The world reaction has no idea the director exists. Conditions come in, it spreads by rules, and it\nkeeps the list of live events up to date."],[99,"This project follows Keep a Changelog and\nSemantic Versioning."],[330,"Threat accumulation / stress decay"],[84,"Threat signal (swappable)"],[275,"Throws an ember into dry grass upwind → it rides the wind toward the player"],[334,"Time constants for rising / falling"],[235,"Tower defense"],[274,"Trigger"],[277,"Trigger"],[315,"Tuning — `TensionConfig`"],[135,"Two games inspired it:"],[117,"Unity **2022.3** or newer"],[119,"Unity Package Manager → **Add package from git URL**:"],[81,"Update tension"],[282,"Use `DefaultDirectorBrain` to run with no overrides."],[307,"Use the editor's **Tools → Tempo → Debug Window** to watch the tension graph, phase, event count and\nburning cells live. Wire it up from your game code:"],[325,"Value"],[5,"Value types"],[209,"Vampire Survivors / Survivor.io / Archero — an AI director that auto-paces wave intensity."],[332,"Weights when combining the two signals"],[130,"What Tempo does"],[254,"When the line is too easy (low tension) the director seeds rushes/special mobs to squeeze; when it's\noverwhelmed (high) it gives breathing room. \"Elemental combos\" — luring a shock onto a freeze field the\nplayer laid down — fall out of the same table naturally."],[123,"When the player is hit, spike the tension immediately."],[288,"With a single threshold the phase flickers at the boundary. So the enter and exit thresholds differ\n(hysteresis), and a minimum relax time is guaranteed."],[143,"World reaction"],[337,"World reaction"],[157,"World reaction · Director · Tension · Safeguards"],[126,"World reaction for the spread rules in depth."],[112,"Your first loop"]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":31,"2":32,"3":33,"4":34,"5":35,"6":36,"7":37,"8":38,"9":39,"10":40,"11":41,"12":42,"13":43,"14":44,"15":45,"16":46,"17":47,"18":48,"19":49,"20":50,"21":51,"22":52,"23":53,"24":54,"25":55,"26":56,"27":57,"28":58,"29":59,"30":60,"31":61,"32":62,"33":63,"34":64,"35":65,"36":66,"37":67,"38":68,"39":69,"40":70,"41":71,"42":72,"43":73,"44":74,"45":75,"46":76,"47":77,"48":78,"49":79,"50":80,"51":81,"52":82,"53":83,"54":84,"55":85,"56":86,"57":87,"58":88,"59":89,"60":90,"61":91,"62":92,"63":93,"64":94,"65":95,"66":96,"67":97,"68":98,"69":99,"70":100,"71":101,"72":102,"73":103,"74":104,"75":105,"76":106,"77":107,"78":108,"79":109,"80":110,"81":111,"82":112,"83":113,"84":114,"85":115,"86":116,"87":117,"88":118,"89":119,"90":120,"91":121,"92":122,"93":123,"94":124,"95":125,"96":126,"97":127,"98":128,"99":129,"100":130,"101":131,"102":132,"103":133,"104":134,"105":135,"106":136,"107":137,"108":237,"109":238,"110":239,"111":240,"112":241,"113":242,"114":243,"115":244,"116":245,"117":246,"118":247,"119":248,"120":249,"121":250,"122":251,"123":252,"124":253,"125":254,"126":255,"127":256,"128":0,"129":1,"130":2,"131":3,"132":4,"133":5,"134":6,"135